      "content": "g/wiki/Actress \"Actress\") and [dancer](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dance \"Dance\"), best known for her roles as [matriarch Emily Gilmore](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emily_Gilmore \"Emily Gilmore\") on the series _[Gilmore Girls](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gilmore_Girls \"Gilmore Girls\")_ and as Marjorie Houseman, the mother of [Jennifer Grey](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jennifer_Grey \"Jennifer Grey\")'s Frances \"Baby\" Houseman, in the film _[Dirty Dancing](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dirty_Dancing \"Dirty Dancing\")_. Bishop originated the role of Sheila in _[A Chorus Line](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/A_Chorus_Line \"A Chorus Line\")_ for which she won a [Tony Award for Best Performance by a Featured Actress in a Musical](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tony_Award_for_Best_Performance_by_a_Featured_Actress_in_a_Musical \"Tony Award for Best Performance by a Featured Actress in a Musical\"). In 2023, she starred as Mrs. Ivey in _[The Watchful Eye](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Watchful_Eye \"The Watchful Eye\")_ (2023).\n## Early life\n[[edit](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Kelly_Bishop&action=edit&section=1 \"Edit section: Early life\")]\nBishop was born on February 28, 1944, in [Colorado Springs](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Colorado_Springs,_Colorado \"Colorado Springs, Colorado\"), [Colorado](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Colorado \"Colorado\").[[2]](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kelly_Bishop#cite_note-2) She grew up in [Denver](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Denver \"Denver\"), [Colorado](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Colorado \"Colorado\"), where she trained to be a [ballet dancer](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ballerina \"Ballerina\"), and as a teenager, moved to California attending the [San Jose Ballet](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/San_Jose_Ballet \"San Jose Ballet\") School. At 18, she headed to [New York City](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_York_City \"New York City\") and landed her first job dancing in a year-round [ballet company](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ballet_company \"Ballet company\") at [Radio City Music Hall](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Radio_City_Music_Hall \"Radio City Music Hall\"). Bishop continued to dance in [Las Vegas](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Las_Vegas_Valley \"Las Vegas Valley\"), [summer stock](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Summer_stock_theatre \"Summer stock theatre\"), and on television until she was cast in 1967 in _[Gold",
